  "description": "The Android engine for CodeBrix.VideoProcessing.Core: analyse media files, decode video frames (I420, NV12, RGBA or Gray, at 8 bits or - where the device decoder outputs 10-bit P010 - 10 bits) and audio samples, write standard MP4 video (H.264, or HEVC where the device has an encoder, with AAC audio and a fast-start index) from your own frames and sound, take snapshots, and transcode, trim and join files - all on Android's own MediaExtractor, MediaCodec and MediaMuxer, with no native code and no ffmpeg. For .NET 10 Android applications on API level 33 and newer; register it once with CodeBrixVideoProcessingAndroid.Register() and code written against CodeBrix.VideoProcessing.Core works unchanged.",
